\begin{align*}
AG^2 &= AE^2 + AD^2 + AB^2 \\
BH^2 &= AB^2 + AE^2 + AD^2 \\
CE^2 &= AD^2 + AB^2 + AE^2 \\
DF^2 &= AB^2 + AD^2 + AE^2.
\end{align*}
The sum of these squares is:
\begin{align*}
AG^2 + BH^2 + CE^2 + DF^2 &= 4(AB^2 + AD^2 + AE^2).
\end{align*}
